# Anti-lag smoothing rework (2026-10-16)

- Decoupled simulation work cost from start-to-start tick cadence. The adaptive scheduler's deliberate wait no longer feeds back into load detection or triggers false emergency mitigation.
- Added a configurable exponential moving average for cycle cost and event-loop delay (`RANAR_LOAD_RUNTIME_EMA_ALPHA`, default `0.30`). Raw extreme stalls and critical memory pressure still bypass the smoothing window.
- Made natural-population recounts incremental (`RANAR_LAG_POPULATION_RECOUNT_BATCH_SIZE`, default `500` entities per cycle), avoiding periodic full-world scans. The last completed count is reused until a new bounded scan finishes; natural spawns fail closed under load while the initial population count is incomplete.
- Shortened staged recovery hysteresis to five healthy samples by default (`RANAR_LOAD_RECOVERY_SAMPLES`), stepping down one severity tier at a time.
- Added tests for scheduler-feedback prevention, smoothed escalation/recovery, emergency detection, and bounded population recounts.


# Stability and lifecycle fixes (2026-10-10)

- Fixed standalone entity team initialization: root entities now retain their own team ID instead of inheriting `undefined` from themselves. This addresses an entity-state defect that could leave entities outside normal team/combat handling.
- Delayed destructive lag contingencies until the configured lag duration is sustained. The unknown-entity cleanup sweep now waits for the 100ms persistence window, and critical entity suspension waits 15 seconds by default (`RANAR_LAG_CRITICAL_DURATION_MS`).
- Hardened WebSocket cleanup against duplicate close/error events, forced termination after transport errors, and ensured delayed disconnect cleanup only targets the original departing body.
- Added regression tests for lag persistence and the adaptive game-loop scheduler.
